---
import PolicyLayout from '@/components/policy/PolicyLayout.astro';
import { fetchGlobal } from '@/lib/global';

const global = await fetchGlobal();
const email = global?.generalEmail ?? 'externalaffairs@empower.org.ki';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Website Privacy Policy"
  subtitle="How Empower Kiribati collects, manages, uses, and safeguards information obtained through our website, digital programs, and infrastructure."
  description="How Empower Kiribati collects, uses, and safeguards personal information under the Kiribati Data Protection Act 2025, and how to make a privacy request."
>
  <h2>1. Overview &amp; Commitment</h2>
  <p>
    As a digital-first social impact organization, Empower Kiribati recognizes that data security is
    not merely a technical requirement, but a fundamental pillar of our commitment to safeguarding
    and human rights. We promote safe practices across the organization to model excellence in
    digital safety, safeguard access to personal and organizational data, and protect the security
    and privacy of all data subjects.
  </p>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy sets out how Empower Kiribati collects, manages, uses, and safeguards
    information obtained through our website, digital programs, and infrastructure.
  </p>
  <div class="policy-table">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Policy overview element</th>
          <th scope="col">Standards &amp; commitments</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Organization</th>
          <td>Empower Kiribati (Te Kimatore CS Compound, Bikenibeu, South Tarawa)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Core Governing Law</th>
          <td>Kiribati Data Protection Act 2025</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Oversight Roles</th>
          <td>Technology Steward &amp; Compliance Lead</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Scope</th>
          <td>All Partners, Contractors, Volunteers, and Program Participants</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>2. Information Collection &amp; Usage</h2>
  <p>
    Empower Kiribati adheres strictly to principles of purpose limitation and data minimization
    across all operations.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Purpose Limitation:</strong> Any identifiable participant information collected by the
      organization is kept secure and used exclusively for the specific purpose for which it was
      originally collected.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Data Minimization:</strong> Organizational roles are explicitly restricted to collecting
      only the participant data strictly required to fulfill a given project's defined objective.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Transparency Exclusion:</strong> Personal identifiable participant data is strictly excluded
      from standard organizational transparency practices to preserve individual privacy.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Protection of Children &amp; Vulnerable Participants</h2>
  <p>
    Empower Kiribati maintains a dedicated framework to protect the welfare, rights, and privacy of
    children, youth, women, and other vulnerable groups in all digital and physical environments.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Data Collection Limits for Minors:</strong> Personal data for individuals under the age of
      18 or those otherwise lacking legal capacity can only be collected for the specific purposes of
      educational programs and for no other reason.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Encrypted Domain Storage:</strong> Notwithstanding standard operational transparency, all
      sensitive records and personal data concerning vulnerable persons must be stored within a
      dedicated Encrypted Domain.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Safeguarding &amp; International Alignment:</strong> All digital handling of participant
      data must comply with international conventions, the
      <a href="/safety-of-vulnerable-persons">Safeguard of Vulnerable Persons Policy</a>, and Kiribati
      national child welfare and family protection legislation.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Anonymization &amp; Public Reporting</h2>
  <p>
    To balance public accountability with individual privacy, Empower Kiribati enforces systematic
    data anonymization.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Public Impact Metrics:</strong> Any data compiled for public impact reporting, program
      evaluation, or general communications must be rendered fully anonymous prior to publication.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Re-identification Safeguards:</strong> Anonymization processes are designed to guarantee
      that no individual data subject can be re-identified from general metrics or shared reports.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Data Security &amp; Cybersafety Standards</h2>
  <p>
    All partners, contractors, and volunteers performing accountabilities on behalf of Empower
    Kiribati are subject to rigorous technical and operational security controls.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Eligibility &amp; Access Control:</strong> Digital access is granted strictly on a
      role-accountability basis. All role fillers must complete the organization's mandatory
      Cybersafety Induction learning program prior to access authorization.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Authentication &amp; Password Hygiene:</strong> Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) is
      mandatory for all organizational accounts, including email, shared workspace platforms, and data
      repositories. Password reuse across organizational systems is strictly forbidden, and all
      credentials must be generated and stored using the organization's designated password manager.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Device Protection:</strong> Any physical device used to fulfill accountabilities on behalf
      of the organization is required to run an approved virus protection software.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Third-Party Software Review:</strong> A mandatory security review must be conducted by the
      Technology Steward for any proposed new software or digital tool to verify that the provider
      meets organizational privacy standards.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Incident Response &amp; Breach Notification</h2>
  <p>
    Empower Kiribati maintains active incident detection and swift escalation protocols to address
    any potential security compromises.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Internal Escalation Window:</strong> If a partner suspects a data breach, loses a device
      containing organizational data, or receives a suspicious message, they must report the incident
      directly to the Technology Steward within 2 to 4 hours rather than waiting for standard meeting
      cycles.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Transparent Communication:</strong> In the event of a confirmed data leak or breach, the
      organization prioritizes immediate transparency with affected individuals.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal Alignment:</strong> Incident mitigation and notification protocols operate in full
      compliance with the Kiribati Data Protection Act 2025 and international data protection
      standards.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Data Subject Rights &amp; Inquiries</h2>
  <p>
    Data subjects maintain full rights regarding their personal data processed by Empower Kiribati in
    accordance with the Data Protection Act 2025.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Rights of Access &amp; Rectification:</strong> Data subjects have the right to request
      access to, correction of, or deletion of their personal information maintained by the
      organization.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Privacy Inquiries &amp; Escalations:</strong> For privacy requests, data access inquiries,
      or to submit a security concern, data subjects and website visitors may contact:
    </li>
  </ul>
  <address>
    <strong>Technology Steward / Compliance Lead</strong><br />
    Empower Kiribati (Digital Kiribati Inc)<br />
    Te Kimatore CS Compound, Bikenibeu, South Tarawa<br />
    Website: <a href="https://empower.org.ki">empower.org.ki</a><br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
  </address>
</PolicyLayout>
